## Project Summary

*AI-generated project summary produced by `/write-summary`, for future AI sessions catching up without re-analyzing line-by-line; may be out of date — re-run to refresh.*

### Purpose

Docker launcher for pre-made AI-agent personas. A persona is `agents/<name>.md` (its instructions) plus `<name>.lego` (default tags); a launch builds a layered image and runs the persona's agent CLI in a container as a persistent named instance (`<agent>__<session>`, conversations resume). Beyond solo instances: **clusters** (N agents in one container on one project, talking over a message queue) and **cowork** (a host-side hub relaying between separate containers). Multi-AI by design: Claude Code runs; Gemini CLI builds but cannot start yet.

### Tech Stack

- Python ≥3.12 host code; deps (`pyproject.toml`): `prompt_toolkit` (TUI), `rich` (previews); stdlib otherwise (`tomllib` in, `launch/toml_emit.py` for every hand-written TOML out).
- Plain `docker build` / `docker run`, no compose. Root `Dockerfile` = CLI-less base (debian:trixie-slim, python3, uv, ripgrep, iptables/sudo); every other layer's Dockerfile lives in the tag tree, the harness layer LAST (CLI install, weekly `apt-get upgrade`, the fixed-tier policy bake, ENTRYPOINT).
- Gate: `bash check.sh` = `unittest discover -s launch/tests` + `ruff` + `mypy`; CI only provisions and calls it. One test drives Gemini CLI's own policy engine through node and needs `LAUNCHER_TEST_GEMINI_BUNDLE` (the `[self]` image and CI set it, version pinned in `launch/tests/probes/gemini-cli.version`); unset, it skips and `check.sh` warns.

### The tag system

Six kinds (classes in `launch/tags/`); members are folders under `agents/<kind>/`, each with a TOML `tag.info` (descriptions, `shortname`, optional `[addendum]` for CLAUDE.md, kind fields). `scan_all(AGENTS_DIR)` → `Registry`, validated fail-loud at startup (so `check.sh` covers tree edits).

| Kind | | Member files | Shipped |
|---|---|---|---|
| ai | ⟪ ⟫ | `efforts.tiers` (model + effort per capability standard, `agents/ai/capability.standards`), `models.list` (the models an instance may pick as its default; `model_prefix` in tag.info) | claude, gemini, chatgpt, grok |
| harness | ⟦ ⟧ | `engine.mapping` (budget words → CLI settings), `policy.mapping` (policy words → CLI rules; must state `[fixed]`), `Dockerfile` + `tag.docker` | claude-code, gemini-cli (built); codex-cli, grok-build, hermes, openclaw, opencode (described only) |
| engine | ( ) | `tag.budget` (`effort_tier` + switches/amounts, AI-neutral; nesting overlays) | default, golem, poet, quick, reliable, researcher, thinker, breakthrough |
| profession | [ ] | `Dockerfile` + `tag.docker`; nesting = requires | code, code/webdev, code/self (this repo's dev toolchain) |
| specialty | { } | `warn`, `claude_args`, `workspace_readonly`, `forbid_on` (scopes), `[wants]`; nesting = requires | auto, firewall, dood, read-only, cowork/manager, muxer/cluster/cluster-cowork |
| policy | < > | `tag.rules`: `[allow]`/`[deny]` capabilities (`tools`), shell words and stems, `all`; `[demand] mode`; the table must match `stance` | web-research, free-bash, all-actions, no-git, vcs-safe/no-git-write (`<-gw>`, read-only git bar fetch/pull; nesting = requires), no-net, vcs-safe, plan-first, no-sudo (always-on) |

Hidden `_<name>` dirs are assets, not tags: image layers in the profession tree (`_node`, claimed by npm-installed harnesses; `_dood`, `_muxer`, `_cluster`) and policy fragments a same-named specialty claims (`_read-only` rules; `_cowork` / `_cluster-cowork` raw `claude-code.json` hooks).

